WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.012
Spark S Q L does not erase the S Q L ideas we already learned.

00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:11.763
Filters, joins, grouping, windows, null handling, and row grain still matter.

00:00:12.397 --> 00:00:15.592
What changes is the execution environment.

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:22.092
In Postgres, we usually think about one database engine managing tables and indexes.

00:00:22.092 --> 00:00:27.922
In Spark, the work may run across many workers and many data partitions.

00:00:27.922 --> 00:00:35.000
That means a correct query can still be expensive if it scans too much data or causes large shuffles.
